WEBVTT

00:45.045 --> 00:47.131
I'm going to try to understand
irrational numbers.

00:49.508 --> 00:50.509
Did he mean me?

00:50.593 --> 00:51.427
But why?

00:52.470 --> 00:53.345
What for?

00:54.597 --> 00:55.431
Why on earth?

00:55.514 --> 00:56.557
What?

00:56.640 --> 00:59.185
CHAPTER 29:
SOMETIMES, THE TRUTH CAN BE DANGEROUS

01:00.853 --> 01:02.646
Um, why…

01:04.273 --> 01:08.444
Why would Pythagoras
have killed his student?

01:11.572 --> 01:12.406
Isn't it obvious?

01:13.824 --> 01:17.495
He couldn't bear to see
his world collapse.

01:19.872 --> 01:23.000
5TH CENTURY BC

01:26.921 --> 01:27.922
What is the matter?

01:29.048 --> 01:29.924
Master.

01:30.007 --> 01:31.217
PYTHAGOREAN MATH ACADEMY
CROTON, GREECE

01:31.300 --> 01:32.176
By any chance…

01:32.259 --> 01:33.093
PYTHAGORAS, DIRECTOR

01:33.177 --> 01:35.095
…have you discovered something new?

01:36.138 --> 01:37.765
HIPPASUS, STUDENT

01:37.848 --> 01:39.558
I tried to express the length

01:40.351 --> 01:42.937
of the diagonal of a unit square

01:43.813 --> 01:46.440
as a fraction.

01:46.524 --> 01:49.485
Sure. All numbers can be expressed
as a ratio of integers.

01:49.568 --> 01:51.487
That is the truth
we have always been spreading.

01:52.029 --> 01:52.905
The thing is…

01:55.324 --> 01:57.284
that doesn't seem to hold true.

01:58.035 --> 01:59.036
What did you say?

01:59.578 --> 02:00.663
This number

02:01.497 --> 02:03.749
just cannot be expressed as a fraction.

02:04.542 --> 02:05.584
Wait.

02:06.502 --> 02:07.336
Just a moment.

02:10.840 --> 02:11.924
Fine.

02:12.800 --> 02:13.676
Prove it.

02:20.558 --> 02:21.684
This is a square.

02:22.393 --> 02:23.310
Please look closely.

02:31.193 --> 02:33.696
It just does not work.

02:38.909 --> 02:40.202
If your theory is valid,

02:40.786 --> 02:44.373
then everything
we hold to be true is false.

02:47.751 --> 02:48.627
Have you…

02:50.671 --> 02:51.922
shared this with anyone?

02:52.965 --> 02:56.218
I have not told anyone yet.

02:56.302 --> 02:58.470
I wanted to tell you first, Master.

03:00.639 --> 03:01.473
Good.

03:02.266 --> 03:03.309
That is fortunate.

03:05.644 --> 03:07.104
Hippasus.

03:10.107 --> 03:11.108
Yes?

03:11.692 --> 03:12.943
Let us pretend

03:14.153 --> 03:15.446
your proof never existed.

03:19.158 --> 03:20.075
Master.

03:20.159 --> 03:23.412
Sometimes, the truth can be dangerous.

03:25.998 --> 03:27.166
Master!

03:34.381 --> 03:37.718
The existence of irrational numbers
would have threatened the world order.

03:40.387 --> 03:42.848
Gosh. What a math nerd.

03:42.932 --> 03:45.559
Why does he get a gleam in his eye
whenever he goes over math stuff?

03:45.643 --> 03:46.644
It's freaky.

03:51.023 --> 03:52.358
But still…

03:54.568 --> 03:57.279
it is kind of attractive.

04:07.039 --> 04:07.873
Are you okay?

04:10.250 --> 04:12.836
Yes, I'm fine.

04:14.088 --> 04:16.340
That's what happens
when you keep daydreaming.

04:17.091 --> 04:17.925
Yes.

04:18.676 --> 04:19.843
So embarrassing.

04:20.594 --> 04:22.554
Please, I've seen far worse.

04:26.141 --> 04:28.060
They say suffering embarrassment

04:28.143 --> 04:30.020
boosts your creativity.

04:30.104 --> 04:31.355
I see.

04:31.438 --> 04:34.817
So you're doing it deliberately?
What more have you got in store?

04:35.651 --> 04:37.903
Why would I share it and lessen the blow?

04:37.987 --> 04:40.114
Fine, work on your creativity.

04:40.739 --> 04:41.824
I'll be rooting for you.

04:47.204 --> 04:48.038
EPISODE 9

04:48.122 --> 04:49.456
I'm home.

04:50.082 --> 04:52.292
Hit the bathroom
before you do anything else.

04:53.627 --> 04:54.461
No, I'm good.

04:55.045 --> 04:57.047
I know you can't go when you're out.

04:57.131 --> 05:00.384
From now on, go take a dump
as soon as you get home.

05:00.467 --> 05:03.262
I mean, when nature calls,

05:03.345 --> 05:05.389
don't hold it in. Answer it straightaway.

05:06.181 --> 05:08.142
Okay already.

05:08.225 --> 05:09.727
I can take care of myself.

05:09.810 --> 05:11.895
Why are you fussing about me pooping?

05:11.979 --> 05:14.064
Obviously because
you're not taking good care of yourself!

05:16.358 --> 05:17.609
Fine.

05:18.444 --> 05:19.319
I'm going.

05:21.447 --> 05:24.199
Should I go and see your homeroom teacher?

05:25.075 --> 05:26.243
Why?

05:27.494 --> 05:29.872
He carried you all the way to the ER.

05:29.955 --> 05:32.458
I'm both sorry and grateful.

05:33.042 --> 05:34.918
Oh, no. There's no need for that.

05:35.002 --> 05:36.211
I already thanked him.

05:36.295 --> 05:38.255
He's swamped as is. Don't disturb him.

05:38.338 --> 05:39.631
Promise me you won't, okay?

05:40.299 --> 05:42.051
I guess he's got you good.

05:42.801 --> 05:45.220
But then again,
he's given you all those demerits.

05:45.721 --> 05:47.097
No wonder you're scared stiff of him.

05:47.181 --> 05:49.475
Gosh, he must be quite the hard-ass.

05:50.309 --> 05:51.935
You're in for a tough time.

05:52.019 --> 05:54.605
Well, he's not that bad.

05:54.688 --> 05:57.357
He's just a bit blunt.

05:57.441 --> 06:01.236
He's a bit on the prickly side,

06:01.320 --> 06:03.405
but he's not a bad guy…

06:03.489 --> 06:05.949
Sometimes he can be childish and immature,

06:06.033 --> 06:07.659
but he's not a bad guy at heart.

06:07.743 --> 06:08.827
…at heart.

06:29.973 --> 06:31.016
I get it now.

06:31.100 --> 06:34.728
They say smart people
are masters of manipulation.

06:35.562 --> 06:36.897
There we have it.

06:36.980 --> 06:39.191
I'm being manipulated.

06:39.274 --> 06:41.235
Just like Mr. Yoon.

06:42.194 --> 06:44.029
When you're scolded
and yelled at ten times,

06:44.113 --> 06:45.656
one kind comment will make you go,

06:45.739 --> 06:48.117
"Wait, maybe he's not so bad after all."

06:48.200 --> 06:49.868
Yes, that's exactly it.

06:54.331 --> 06:56.959
Seriously though,
he's been so mean to me all this time.

06:57.042 --> 07:00.045
The jerk says he'd try to understand me,
then my heart skips a beat?

07:00.129 --> 07:01.130
How ridiculous!

07:06.176 --> 07:08.428
Pull yourself together, Eui-ju.

07:08.512 --> 07:11.098
Starting tomorrow, don't even look at him.

07:15.435 --> 07:18.730
CHAPTER 30:
SOMEONE I SHOULDN'T AND CAN'T LIKE

07:22.192 --> 07:23.026
Hey, did you see?

07:23.610 --> 07:25.445
That thing I sent in our group chat.

07:25.529 --> 07:27.656
About Professor Na Deul-i at Princeton

07:27.739 --> 07:30.742
becoming the first Korean
to be awarded the Fields Medal.

07:30.826 --> 07:33.287
What about it? Do you know her?

07:33.996 --> 07:34.872
No, I don't.

07:35.497 --> 07:36.874
But Woo-su does.

07:38.959 --> 07:40.836
She was on his Olympiad team
back in middle school.

07:42.045 --> 07:43.046
Really?

07:43.130 --> 07:44.506
Aren't you jealous?

07:45.174 --> 07:47.301
Don't you think that should have been you?

07:50.095 --> 07:52.764
If only you hadn't dropped out
of the Olympiad.

07:53.891 --> 07:55.851
If you had only studied abroad--

07:56.643 --> 07:57.811
What's wrong?

07:58.437 --> 08:00.022
I thought he was going places.

08:00.731 --> 08:01.940
I had no idea he'd end up here,

08:02.024 --> 08:04.568
bickering with math idiots like you
over toast with me.

08:05.694 --> 08:07.321
I'm talking about my friend Woo-su.

08:07.905 --> 08:09.948
Woo-su, my freaking genius buddy.

08:12.075 --> 08:14.036
Whatever. Forget it.

08:14.536 --> 08:16.872
-He could've won the Fields Medal and--
-Hey.

08:17.456 --> 08:18.498
Give it a rest.

08:19.833 --> 08:21.835
What's so special about some dumb medal?

08:24.922 --> 08:25.797
Hey.

08:26.590 --> 08:28.342
Do you even know what the Fields Medal is?

08:29.593 --> 08:30.427
Of course, I do.

08:30.510 --> 08:33.305
Then tell me who the first recipient was.

08:38.685 --> 08:39.561
David Copperfield.

08:39.645 --> 08:40.687
Forget it.

08:40.771 --> 08:43.523
Why should I bother
talking to someone so ignorant?

08:44.483 --> 08:45.400
Anyhow, Woo-su, you're…

08:48.153 --> 08:49.529
I won't bother with you either.

08:50.239 --> 08:51.406
Enjoy your toast.

08:59.790 --> 09:01.291
When is he going to come out?

09:03.335 --> 09:05.045
It's normally about now.

09:05.712 --> 09:07.089
Do I have everything I need?

09:07.172 --> 09:08.715
Did I bring all my textbooks?

09:08.799 --> 09:10.634
I'd better wear my puffer jacket.

09:10.717 --> 09:12.094
Why isn't he here already?

09:12.177 --> 09:13.387
We're going to be late.

09:14.638 --> 09:15.806
Da-ju, get a move on.

09:15.889 --> 09:17.224
Woo-su left an hour ago.

09:17.307 --> 09:19.142
Jeez, he's a real pain in the neck.

09:19.226 --> 09:20.644
-What on earth?
-What time is it?

09:20.727 --> 09:22.145
We're late for sure.

09:22.229 --> 09:23.897
Jeez, he's always like this.

09:24.940 --> 09:25.941
Isn't that Eui-ju?

09:27.025 --> 09:28.318
Eui-ju?

09:28.402 --> 09:29.403
She'll be late too.

09:34.533 --> 09:37.077
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

09:37.160 --> 09:38.537
Good morning.

09:39.538 --> 09:42.332
Why is he doing that with his hair?

09:42.416 --> 09:43.834
Let's get started.

09:44.960 --> 09:46.753
Why has he pushed his sleeves up?

09:49.464 --> 09:51.216
Why are his fingers so long?

10:02.853 --> 10:05.814
Why is he drinking water like that?

10:10.110 --> 10:11.653
The way he's twiddling his pen…

10:14.823 --> 10:15.699
It's so…

10:17.576 --> 10:18.410
It's so…

10:19.202 --> 10:20.245
So obnoxious.

10:24.166 --> 10:25.709
What is it you want to tell me?

10:26.376 --> 10:27.461
Let's take a seat here.

10:32.758 --> 10:33.800
Go-ya.

10:33.884 --> 10:38.180
Fangirling used to be my only joy in life.

10:38.847 --> 10:39.723
I know.

10:40.849 --> 10:44.728
Of course, many were fictional characters,

10:44.811 --> 10:46.813
but my love for them

10:46.897 --> 10:48.732
was always genuine.

10:49.816 --> 10:51.735
Thinking about those characters

10:51.818 --> 10:53.779
gave me the strength to carry on.

10:54.738 --> 10:55.864
But now…

10:56.615 --> 10:58.867
The fact he keeps cropping up in my mind…

11:00.827 --> 11:01.828
It makes me mad.

11:02.746 --> 11:04.623
The thing is…

11:05.415 --> 11:07.000
I don't want to think about him.

11:07.084 --> 11:09.836
I shouldn't think about him,

11:09.920 --> 11:11.338
but I can't help myself.

11:13.215 --> 11:14.257
You're in denial.

11:15.967 --> 11:16.843
In denial?

11:16.927 --> 11:18.428
You're always like this.

11:18.512 --> 11:21.765
You watch countless videos of some idol
while claiming not to be a fan

11:22.432 --> 11:25.060
or save a gazillion photos
of the lead actor in some series

11:25.143 --> 11:26.812
but say you only watch the show
for his acting.

11:28.063 --> 11:30.232
Do I really?

11:30.315 --> 11:31.942
Yes, you do.

11:32.776 --> 11:35.821
Even when you're into someone,
you don't want to admit it.

11:35.904 --> 11:38.532
No matter how much you deny it,
you're already into him.

11:38.615 --> 11:40.075
No way.

11:41.368 --> 11:42.828
That can't be it.

11:43.412 --> 11:46.123
No. I shouldn't even like him,

11:46.998 --> 11:47.874
and I just can't.

11:48.583 --> 11:49.793
Why not?

11:49.876 --> 11:50.752
Huh?

11:52.379 --> 11:54.798
Why can't you like Mr. Jung?

11:59.469 --> 12:00.303
What?

12:01.471 --> 12:03.849
Why are you in denial about liking him?

12:05.934 --> 12:06.810
Oh…

12:09.438 --> 12:10.772
It's not like that.

12:10.856 --> 12:11.690
No.

12:12.983 --> 12:14.067
-Shall we get going?
-What?

12:14.151 --> 12:15.694
You solved my problem. Let's go.

12:15.777 --> 12:17.571
-Huh?
-Let's go. I'm good now.

12:19.114 --> 12:20.240
Oh. Hey, Jenny.

12:20.323 --> 12:21.366
Where are you going?

12:21.450 --> 12:22.784
Oh, the teachers' office.

12:22.868 --> 12:25.704
I'm gonna apply for a field trip.

12:25.787 --> 12:27.622
I'm so jealous. Where are you going to go?

12:27.706 --> 12:30.542
I'll dress up in hanbok
and visit the Gyeongbokgung Palace.

12:30.625 --> 12:31.877
And then… The market.

12:31.960 --> 12:34.129
I'm going to try gimbap
and tteokbokki there.

12:34.212 --> 12:37.215
Then on to Hongdae before heading
to the Han River to eat ramyeon.

12:37.299 --> 12:38.800
Finally, I'll check out
Namsan Seoul Tower.

12:41.219 --> 12:43.430
Are you sure you have the energy

12:43.513 --> 12:44.723
to do all that in one day?

12:44.806 --> 12:46.475
-Sure.
-But Jenny,

12:46.558 --> 12:48.768
you do know you have to write a report
when you get back, right?

12:48.852 --> 12:50.645
Of course.

12:50.729 --> 12:53.482
"I learned a lot about Korean culture."

12:53.565 --> 12:55.025
That should cover it, no?

12:55.609 --> 12:56.568
Bye!

12:58.528 --> 13:01.781
I guess no one has shown her
the report form yet.

13:02.365 --> 13:04.242
Leave her be. She looks so happy.

13:04.326 --> 13:05.744
I guess. Goodness.

13:05.827 --> 13:08.538
THE DANCING CARNATION
NOTABLE WORK "MY MOTHER" BY YOON DONG-JU

13:22.928 --> 13:23.762
Wow.

13:24.262 --> 13:25.764
Are you reading that again?

13:26.389 --> 13:28.266
You must have it memorized by now.

13:28.350 --> 13:29.184
Of course.

13:29.809 --> 13:32.187
"On the face of the woman
who no longer smiles,

13:32.270 --> 13:34.814
a single flower in full bloom emerged."

13:35.524 --> 13:39.069
Maybe Dong-ju's mother is not smiling
because she passed away.

13:39.861 --> 13:42.489
"And another small flower
that doesn't answer."

13:42.572 --> 13:45.742
The small flower
is probably Dong-ju himself.

13:47.160 --> 13:49.788
Why didn't he answer
when his mother called him?

13:50.413 --> 13:52.040
Why didn't he look at her?

13:52.958 --> 13:54.793
Probably out of resentment, right?

13:55.835 --> 13:58.421
He must regret that so much now.

14:00.006 --> 14:01.049
You know what?

14:01.633 --> 14:03.385
If you'd put this much effort
into your studies,

14:03.468 --> 14:04.844
you'd be crushing Korean Literature.

14:07.097 --> 14:08.682
How are you getting on with your poem?

14:09.683 --> 14:10.517
Well…

14:13.853 --> 14:14.688
Hey.

14:14.771 --> 14:15.772
It's Mr. Yoon.

14:19.276 --> 14:20.694
Hello.

15:05.905 --> 15:06.781
Hey.

15:06.865 --> 15:08.658
Why didn't you come over and say hi?

15:11.036 --> 15:12.871
You two have gotten really close.

15:14.497 --> 15:16.124
Not at all.

15:16.207 --> 15:17.709
He just gave me feedback on my poem.

15:28.553 --> 15:30.513
I shouldn't even like him,

15:31.389 --> 15:32.349
and I just can't.

15:41.232 --> 15:43.443
That's what happens
when you keep daydreaming.

15:45.278 --> 15:46.571
His voice

15:47.405 --> 15:50.325
was definitely full of concern.

15:54.788 --> 15:56.623
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 6

15:59.709 --> 16:02.462
You're the future head
of the family company,

16:03.213 --> 16:04.589
and you're carrying on

16:05.674 --> 16:07.592
with some guy?

16:07.676 --> 16:09.511
Are you out of your mind?

16:09.594 --> 16:11.888
Who told you that? Who would dare…

16:16.935 --> 16:18.144
It was me, Si-on.

16:20.271 --> 16:21.272
I did it for you.

16:21.856 --> 16:22.691
You?

16:24.818 --> 16:25.860
So you joined the company

16:25.944 --> 16:29.030
to get close to my mom and rat me out
about my relationship with Yoon?

16:29.948 --> 16:31.908
I was only looking out for your future.

16:33.410 --> 16:35.036
You're destined for great things.

16:36.579 --> 16:38.415
You can't afford to set tongues wagging.

16:39.457 --> 16:40.750
Don't make me laugh.

16:41.418 --> 16:44.379
You think if you break us up,
he'll run into your arms?

16:44.462 --> 16:45.547
He was the first person

16:46.673 --> 16:47.924
to laugh at my jokes.

16:48.007 --> 16:49.217
You've got to be kidding me.

16:49.843 --> 16:52.345
He laughed at my jokes.

16:53.096 --> 16:55.098
To spare your feelings, no doubt.
He's kind that way.

16:55.181 --> 16:57.225
No, that's not it.

16:57.851 --> 16:58.852
You have no idea

16:58.935 --> 17:01.730
about the way he looks at me.

17:01.813 --> 17:04.399
He doesn't look at anyone else that way.

17:04.482 --> 17:05.525
-It's the same.
-No.

17:05.608 --> 17:06.568
-Exactly the same.
-No…

17:08.486 --> 17:10.905
You're welcome
to take your anger out on me.

17:10.989 --> 17:12.782
But if you touch him, I won't let it go.

17:17.036 --> 17:19.622
-No, I won't let you pass.
-Get out of my way.

17:19.706 --> 17:21.458
No. Never…

17:22.167 --> 17:24.335
-Mr. Kim!
-Yes, ma'am.

17:28.173 --> 17:29.632
Lock him up until that Choi Yoon

17:29.716 --> 17:31.885
or whatever his name is dealt with.

17:35.805 --> 17:37.682
Let go. Let go of me!

17:45.231 --> 17:46.191
Get him!

18:51.631 --> 18:52.465
Are you okay?

18:53.049 --> 18:55.385
What did I tell you
about wandering off alone, Yoon?

18:56.803 --> 18:57.846
Are you hurt?

19:06.563 --> 19:07.522
Let's go.

19:19.492 --> 19:21.494
Shoot, what was that about?

19:23.538 --> 19:25.582
Why did Yoon turn into a self-insert?

19:25.665 --> 19:27.000
Why did I replace Mr. Yoon?

19:28.376 --> 19:30.503
Why was I on fire there?
Everything was so vivid.

19:32.046 --> 19:33.047
No way. Surely not…

19:41.014 --> 19:44.309
TOPOLOGY OF ALGEBRAIC CURVES AND SURFACES

19:50.064 --> 19:51.649
HEY, IT'S BEEN A WHILE

19:51.733 --> 19:53.735
I'M BACK IN KOREA
CAN WE MEET UP?

19:58.948 --> 20:00.450
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

20:17.550 --> 20:18.718
I'll try that.

20:24.766 --> 20:25.683
Go-ya.

20:29.687 --> 20:30.730
We need to talk.

20:38.696 --> 20:39.572
What was that?

20:40.323 --> 20:42.116
Oh, well,

20:42.200 --> 20:45.370
I told Mr. Yoon I was having difficulty
coming up with a title.

20:45.453 --> 20:48.539
He suggested using the first image
that came to mind when I read my poem,

20:48.623 --> 20:51.209
or the word repeated the most in it.

20:51.292 --> 20:54.462
So I tried it,
and I wanted his take on my ideas.

20:54.545 --> 20:55.964
Why did you go by yourself?

20:56.047 --> 20:57.256
You could've taken me along.

20:58.424 --> 21:00.510
I did consider that.

21:00.593 --> 21:02.845
But it was no big deal,
so I went to see him by myself.

21:04.263 --> 21:05.098
"No big deal"?

21:06.349 --> 21:09.686
I'm so nervous around Dong-ju
that I can't even say hi to him.

21:09.769 --> 21:13.022
But for you, laughing and chatting
with him is no big deal?

21:16.943 --> 21:18.361
Well, the thing is…

21:18.861 --> 21:19.862
Tell me the truth.

21:20.822 --> 21:22.365
The guy you like isn't Mr. Jung, is it?

21:23.199 --> 21:24.450
You like Dong-ju, don't you?

21:26.077 --> 21:27.161
What are you talking about?

21:27.245 --> 21:28.454
I'm right, aren't I?

21:28.538 --> 21:30.581
Otherwise, why would you go see him alone?

21:31.165 --> 21:32.375
Why are you in denial?

21:35.253 --> 21:36.504
Wait.

21:36.587 --> 21:38.756
It's not Mr. Yoon.

21:44.345 --> 21:47.724
If it's not him,
why can't you tell me who it is?

21:47.807 --> 21:50.351
You're acting so weird right now.

21:54.063 --> 21:55.106
Don't you trust me?

21:56.649 --> 21:57.483
What?

21:57.567 --> 22:01.029
I told you it's not what you think.
Do you have to keep going on about it?

22:01.654 --> 22:03.656
Have I ever lied to you?

22:07.368 --> 22:08.327
Fine.

22:08.995 --> 22:10.079
I guess you're right.

22:10.163 --> 22:13.624
Maybe I'm so blinded by love
that I can't trust an innocent friend.

22:22.133 --> 22:23.092
Shall I give it a go?

22:23.176 --> 22:25.136
-You think I can do it?
-Shall I do it, then?

22:25.219 --> 22:26.095
Did you get cookies?

22:26.179 --> 22:27.221
Leave me alone.

22:35.938 --> 22:36.773
Hey.

22:37.607 --> 22:38.566
What's up with her?

22:43.071 --> 22:44.572
-You think they argued?
-No doubt.

22:44.655 --> 22:45.656
They argued for sure.

23:08.346 --> 23:10.389
She'll get over it soon, right?

23:28.116 --> 23:33.204
CHAPTER 31:
EVERYONE HAS A SPECIAL SOMEONE

23:48.469 --> 23:49.554
Wait.

23:50.179 --> 23:51.097
What the heck?

23:52.140 --> 23:54.475
Mr. Jung just left.

23:54.559 --> 23:56.018
So why am I waiting for Mr. Ga?

23:58.604 --> 23:59.564
No way.

24:00.148 --> 24:03.025
Just looking at his face makes me sad.

24:03.109 --> 24:03.943
Are you okay?

24:08.865 --> 24:10.032
No way.

24:27.967 --> 24:28.801
Love is…

24:28.885 --> 24:30.386
like the first snow.

24:30.469 --> 24:31.429
Love at first sight.

24:31.929 --> 24:33.598
When you see them,

24:33.681 --> 24:36.392
you know that person is meant for you.

24:37.393 --> 24:39.020
That's how it is, kiddo.

24:42.190 --> 24:43.566
MINI MOCK EXAMINATION 7

24:47.945 --> 24:49.947
My first snow

24:50.031 --> 24:52.158
isn't Mr. Jung but Mr. Ga?

24:55.161 --> 24:56.245
What am I going to do?

24:57.788 --> 25:00.958
What am I going to do?

25:08.049 --> 25:09.508
Your cafe mocha is ready.

25:11.594 --> 25:13.179
Thanks. Enjoy your drink.

25:13.262 --> 25:14.889
Thank you.

25:33.991 --> 25:34.867
What the heck?

25:35.868 --> 25:37.203
What's he doing here?

25:39.705 --> 25:41.040
Why didn't I see him earlier?

25:41.123 --> 25:43.626
When I ordered this earlier…

25:43.709 --> 25:45.378
At the counter…

25:47.046 --> 25:48.172
I can't believe this.

25:49.924 --> 25:53.344
Wait, did he see me
and come in on purpose?

25:53.427 --> 25:54.387
My goodness.

25:55.429 --> 25:56.305
Or maybe not.

25:57.390 --> 25:59.141
Is this what they call fate?

26:03.145 --> 26:04.105
Huh?

26:06.565 --> 26:07.733
Cafe mocha?

26:13.406 --> 26:14.573
It doesn't suit him at all.

26:15.491 --> 26:17.326
He's got so much whipped cream on it.

26:18.077 --> 26:20.871
What the heck? He has it just like I do.

26:21.706 --> 26:22.748
What is he playing at?

26:27.128 --> 26:28.587
Who is he waving at?

26:38.889 --> 26:40.016
Long time no see.

26:40.099 --> 26:42.101
I've missed you so much.

26:45.271 --> 26:47.898
Until then,
I didn't understand my own feelings.

26:48.816 --> 26:49.775
But in that moment,

26:50.776 --> 26:52.445
everything became crystal clear.

26:56.032 --> 26:59.410
My heart had been running wild,
without direction or plan,

27:00.036 --> 27:01.203
and I finally understood it.

27:03.247 --> 27:04.790
Everyone…

27:06.375 --> 27:07.793
has a special someone

27:08.377 --> 27:11.547
who makes their heart sink at least once.

28:19.698 --> 28:21.700
Subtitle: Paul Carver
